# Modelfile for serving talkie-1930 in Ollama *with system-prompt support*.
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES
# ------------------
# Ollama's auto-generated template for talkie-1930 was:
#
#     <|user|>{{ .Prompt }}<|end|><|assistant|>
#
# There is no <|system|> slot in it, so any system prompt passed via
# `ollama run talkie-1930 --system "..."` (or the API `system` field) is
# silently DISCARDED before it ever reaches the model — not resisted, dropped.
#
# talkie's real chat format (see src/talkie/chat.py:format_chat) does have a
# system role. The template below wires it back up so the system prompt is
# rendered into the prompt the model actually sees.
#
# USAGE
# -----
#   # Requires the base `talkie-1930` model already imported into Ollama via the
#   # TalkieForCausalLM architecture port (see CLAUDE.md → "Running on Apple Silicon").
#   ollama create talkie-1930-sys -f Modelfile
#   ollama run talkie-1930-sys --system "Thou art a sentimental poet." "What is the wireless telephone?"
#
# NOTE: a persona only steers talkie if 1930 contained one. "Poet" or "minister"
# work; "Silicon Valley engineer" gets ignored because the corpus has no such word.

FROM talkie-1930

TEMPLATE """{{ if .System }}<|system|>{{ .System }}<|end|>{{ end }}<|user|>{{ .Prompt }}<|end|><|assistant|>"""

PARAMETER stop <|end|>
PARAMETER stop <|endoftext|>
PARAMETER stop <|user|>
PARAMETER stop <|system|>
